From d3b272fb8be99717eab65834f68e76cf19580aab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Captain Polliwog build <build@captainpolliwog.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:57:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 42/58] CSS: gap for flexbox, column-gap/row-gap/gap for grid,
 logical properties, inset, :has(), overflow: clip

- Flexbox lays out column-gap and row-gap between items and lines.
- column-gap also sets grid's gap; row-gap and gap are grid-row-gap and
  grid-gap; 'normal' is accepted.
- padding-/margin-inline and -block (shorthands and longhands), border-
  inline/block sides, inline-size, block-size and their min/max, inset,
  inset-inline, inset-block. var() in the logical shorthands resolves after
  the cascade turns them physical.
- :has() with relative selectors; elements it matched are restyled when
  their contents, attributes or checked state change, and don't share style.
- overflow: clip (drawn as hidden, without making the other axis scroll)
  and two-value overflow.
- The pseudo-class name table is regenerated when its .in file changes.
